The paper presents a novel PAC-Bayes generalization bound for neural network ensembles, which is tighter than existing bounds and can be applied to any ensemble of neural networks. The bound is based on the notion of a “pseudo-ensemble”, which is a set of neural networks that are trained on different subsets of the training data. The bound is derived by bounding the expected loss of the pseudo-ensemble on the test data, and then using the fact that the expected loss of the pseudo-ensemble is an upper bound on the expected loss of the true ensemble.
The paper also presents a new algorithm for training neural network ensembles, which is based on the idea of “pseudo-ensembles”. The algorithm is shown to be more efficient than existing algorithms, and to achieve better generalization performance.
The paper is a significant contribution to the field of neural network ensembles, and will be of interest to researchers and practitioners in the field.
